{"move_object":{"move":"POINT","confusion":"","confusion_skill":"","highlights":[{"entity_id":789,"end_line":42,"path":"","start_line":34}],"note":"Learner asked for a clear binding-vs-const example. Pointed at syntax.rs lines 34-42 and asked them to predict the two outputs before running. Next turn: check they say line 36 prints 9 (new binding) and line 40 prints 'equal' (const comparison), then confirm C3 looks solid and suggest assessment.","response":"Haan, dono ek hi file me saath hain, isliye best hai wahan se dekhna. `syntax.rs` ki lines 34 se 42 tak dekho: line 34 me `let wanted = 5;` hai, aur line 36 me `wanted =>` likha hai, jabki line 40 me `n if n == wanted =>` hai.

